# A block's `fn` that calls one written below it, neither with a signature line and
# neither calling itself (Semantics ch. 4, "Binding groups and cycles": a block's lines
# are one group, in any order; Type System ch. 5, "A local `let` generalizes"). The use
# above decided the type of the name bound ahead, and the checker then read the function
# below as a signed one ("this clause takes one parameter; the signature has no").
# Written by Claude on the claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

Twice: fn Nat -> Nat
fn Twice n:
    fn First k = Second k
    fn Second k = k + k
    First n

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"twice {Twice 4}")
